factors.mechanical_chassis:
### 4.1 Destructive Damage

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- add one Destruction Package to legal damaging effect;
- source attack/save applies;
- damage type must be stated.

### 4.3 Resistance Breach

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- target with Resistance makes save or Destruction Check contests defensive DC;
- on success, Resistance is ignored for this packet;
- on success by 5+, suppress that Resistance until start of next turn;
- immunity unaffected.

### 4.4 Immunity Fracture

**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP, GM-reviewed for strong immunities

Default:

- make Destruction Check against immunity source DC;
- on success, immunity becomes Resistance for this packet;
- on success by 5+, immunity becomes Resistance until start of next turn;
- on failure, immunity holds.

### 4.8 Deny Temporary HP

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- first time each round target would gain temp HP, reduce by one Destruction Package;
- if reduced to 0, temp HP gain fails;
- if target already has temp HP, damage package applies to temp HP first.

### 4.9 Breach Effect

**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default:

- make Destruction Check against effect DC/controller DC;
- on success, suppress ongoing effect until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, reduce duration one step or break minor effect;
- on failure, effect remains.

### 4.10 Deep Breach

**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Default:

- as Breach Effect;
- can affect major ward/seal/domain/fortification layer;
- success by 5+ reduces major layer one stage;
- success by 10+ breaks if no higher authority protects it.

### 4.11 Defense Fracture

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- choose AC bonus, save bonus, damage reduction, shield layer, Fortification Package, Resistance layer, or cover-like created defense;
- on successful breach, reduce by PB or one Destruction Package;
- lasts until start of next turn.

### 4.12 Destructive Imposition

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- after dealing damage, impose one minor ruin rider: lose Reaction, Speed -10 feet, object cracked, armor layer weakened, healing reduced, concentration/maintenance check with penalty;
- target saves if rider is not already tied to failed save/hit;
- lasts until start of next turn.

### 4.13 Area Ruin

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- apply Destructive Damage or Object Ruin in source area;
- each creature saves/defends separately;
- objects/terrain use Object Ruin;
- cannot selectively spare targets without selection source.

### 4.14 Structure-Scale Ruin

**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP, GM-reviewed for major structures

Default:

- target structure segment;
- use Destruction Check against structure Break DC;
- on success, deal doubled Object Ruin package and reduce Break DC/Integrity;
- collapse condition must be stated;
- occupants get save if collapse harms them.

### 4.1 Veil Target

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default effect:

- conceal one target for 1 minute;
- observers must pass Detection Check to advance state;
- direct targeting blocked until Targetable;
- attacking or obvious action may grant observers immediate Detection Check.

### 4.2 Veil Area

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- conceal an area, room, formation, grove, battlefield patch, or route;
- observers outside cannot directly identify contents until reveal;
- creatures inside are not automatically hidden from each other unless Art says so;
- area effects can still enter if target area is guessed or known.

### 4.3 Hidden Origin

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- hide the origin point/source of one effect;
- observer may know effect exists but not source;
- Detection Check success reveals direction/origin state;
- success by 5+ reveals actual origin or source category.

### 4.4 Suppress Signs

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default effect:

- suppress sound, light, scent, aura, casting signs, qi flare, spiritual pressure, blood smell, weapon flash, or formation glow;
- choose signs suppressed;
- duration 1 minute;
- does not hide physical body unless paired with Veil Target.

### 4.5 False Signature

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- replace trace/source/aura with false one;
- observer failing by 5+ on Detection Check receives false result;
- success reveals falsehood;
- success by 5+ reveals true signature category.

### 4.6 Trace Erasure

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- erase or suppress one Trace category in an area or from a target;
- Revelation/Tracking/Investigation against Reveal DC can recover degraded trace;
- success by 5+ recovers direction/time/source category;
- trace erasure does not alter memories unless another source supports that.

### 4.7 Conceal Prepared Effect

**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default effect:

- hide one prepared technique, trap, talisman, formation trigger, stored effect, or delayed art;
- observers cannot identify trigger until Detection Check reaches Analyzed;
- when triggered, effect reveals itself unless Art also hides activation signs;
- hidden prepared effect must still have normal action surface.

### 4.8 Hidden Route

**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default effect:

- conceal path, door, gate, tunnel, shadow route, formation route, spirit road, or transport mark;
- Detection Check reveals Presence/Direction/Location/Targetable as normal;
- Transport through hidden route still requires Transport legality;
- breaking route concealment does not destroy route.

### 4.9 Untargetable Technique

**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Default effect:

- one target gains Direct Targeting Block for 1 minute or until it attacks/uses overt hostile action;
- observers with Targetable state can target normally;
- area effects, environmental hazards, and non-direct effects still work;
- GM review if combined with strong offense and no reveal route.

### 4.1 Temporary HP Fortification

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- target gains one Fortification Package temporary HP;
- lasts 1 minute;
- does not stack with same source unless Art says separate layer;
- ends when depleted or duration expires.

### 4.2 AC Fortification

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- target gains +PB AC or smaller static value for 1 minute;
- no stacking with same source;
- suppressed by Break/Suppression result.

### 4.3 Save Fortification

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- target gains +PB to one save category or one Fortification Die to next save;
- duration 1 minute or until used;
- must state save category.

### 4.4 Resistance Fortification

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- target gains Resistance to one source-supported damage type for 1 minute;
- if target already has Resistance, gain one Fortification Package damage reduction once per round instead;
- immunity requires separate GM-reviewed effect.

### 4.5 Damage Reduction Layer

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- once per round when target takes damage, reduce by one Fortification Package;
- lasts 1 minute;
- if damage reduced to 0, layer may lose one Integrity/use if written.

### 4.6 Object / Structure Reinforcement

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- object/structure gains Integrity equal to one Fortification Package + PB;
- may gain Damage Threshold;
- Break DC increases by PB;
- lasts 1 hour for ritual or 1 minute in combat.

### 4.7 Ward / Seal Reinforcement

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- choose ward/seal/ongoing defense;
- increase Break DC by PB or add Integrity one Fortification Package;
- first successful suppression only suppresses until start of next turn, not break.

### 4.8 Ongoing Effect Fortification

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- protect one ongoing effect from suppression/dispelling/duration erosion;
- first contest against it must also beat Fortification DC;
- on success by 5+ when fortified, duration erosion is reduced one step.

### 4.9 Collapse Delay

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- when protected target/layer would hit 0 Integrity or end by break, delay collapse until start of your next turn;
- if repaired above 0 before then, collapse is prevented;
- once used, delay layer ends.

### 4.1 HP Restoration

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- target regains one Restoration Package HP;
- cannot exceed max HP;
- if anti-healing exists, contest it first.

### 4.2 Max HP Restoration

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- restore max HP reduction by one Restoration Package or PB + Refinement Ability Modifier;
- requires harm category/source;
- major/root max HP pressure may require Soul Repair;
- success by 5+ also restores current HP up to restored maximum if source supports.

### 4.3 Condition Cleansing

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- choose one named condition;
- Restoration Check against condition DC;
- on success, remove minor condition or suppress major condition until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, remove stronger condition if source supports;
- on failure, condition remains but category is confirmed.

### 4.4 Poison / Disease Cleansing

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- make Restoration Check against poison/disease DC;
- on success, end one poison/disease or reduce severity one stage;
- on success by 5+, remove one secondary symptom;
- on failure by 5+, symptom flares or treatment material is consumed.

### 4.5 Curse / Spiritual Contamination Cleansing

**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default:

- make Restoration Check against curse/contamination DC;
- on success, suppress curse/contamination for 1 minute or remove minor curse;
- on success by 5+, remove one major symptom or reveal anchor;
- major curse may need anchor break, Heaven, Soul, or story route.

### 4.6 Deviation / Hidden Injury Symptom Relief

**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default:

- choose one symptom;
- make Restoration Check against symptom DC;
- on success, suppress symptom until next long rest or reduce immediate penalty one stage;
- on success by 5+, create stable treatment route or reduce minor symptom;
- does not erase deep root harm without Soul/GM route.

### 4.7 Object / Structure Repair

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- repair one Restoration Package HP/Integrity;
- cannot restore missing complex function unless Function Restoration is used;
- destroyed object may need Creation/Transformation.

### 4.8 Function Restoration

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- name lost function;
- make Restoration Check against Break/condition/effect DC;
- on success, restore function for 1 minute or until damage recurs;
- on success by 5+, function remains repaired for normal duration.

### 4.9 Ward / Seal / Ongoing Effect Restoration

**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default:

- repair Integrity, restore duration one step, or suppress disruption;
- make Restoration Check against effect DC;
- on success, restore one package/increment;
- on success by 5+, also remove one minor suppression.

### 4.10 Delayed Recovery

**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default:

- create Recovery Window;
- target heals/repairs one Restoration Package at start of next turn or after 10 minutes;
- if target takes same harm before then, recovery requires check or fails.

### 4.11 Emergency Restoration

**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default:

- Reaction when target takes damage, drops to 0, suffers condition, or layer breaks;
- restore one package, suppress harm until start of next turn, or trigger Recovery Window;
- cannot undo death without Soul/Heaven/Life route.

### 5.1 Material Transformation

**Factor:** Material Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Changes one material into a related legal material.

Default effect:

- target object/material up to one 5-foot cube or one carried object;
- unattended target: Transformation Check against material DC if complex;
- attended/unwilling object: holder gets Dexterity or Constitution save;
- duration 1 minute or 1 hour ritual;
- transformed material uses new material traits listed by Art;
- on success by 5+, increase durability by PB or extend duration one step;
- on failure by 5+, unstable material reverts at end of next turn.

Related material examples: water to ice, iron to steel-like spiritual iron, wood to living root, stone to clay, sand to glass, blood to crystal, qi mist to thread.

### 5.2 Deep Material Transformation

**Factor:** Deep Material Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Changes unrelated or spiritually resistant material.

Default effect:

- requires Transformation Check against higher of material DC or Break DC;
- on success, material changes and gains Stable Transformation for duration;
- on success by 5+, one special trait is added if source supports;
- on failure, no change;
- on failure by 5+, backlash or contamination occurs.

Permanent deep material change is GM-reviewed.

### 5.3 Terrain Transformation

**Factor:** Terrain Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Changes terrain.

Default effect:

- area: one 10-foot square or source area;
- duration 1 minute;
- choose terrain mode: difficult, clear, slick, grasping, soft, hard, elevated, lowered, obscuring, fertile, barren, consecrated, corrupted, elemental;
- creatures in area when it appears make Dexterity/Strength save if hazardous or restraining;
- on success, avoid initial rider;
- on failure, rider applies;
- terrain can be suppressed by Transformation Contest.

### 5.4 Hazardous Terrain Transformation

**Factor:** Hazardous Terrain Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Adds hazard to terrain.

Default effect:

- trigger: creature enters or starts turn in area, once per round;
- save: source save or Dexterity/Constitution/Strength;
- on failure, take one Form Package damage or suffer written rider;
- on success, half damage/no rider;
- on failed by 5+, rider lasts until start of creature's next turn.

### 5.5 Body Transformation

**Factor:** Body Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Changes body or body part.

Default effect:

- willing target: no save;
- unwilling target: Constitution save;
- duration 1 minute;
- choose up to two Form Statistics from: movement mode, natural weapon, AC +PB maximum, temporary HP one Form Package, sense, speech change, hands/manipulation change, resistance to one narrow source, size feature without size category change, breathing mode;
- on success by 5+, add one additional minor statistic;
- on failure, no transformation;
- on failed by 5+, target also suffers Reversion Shock when form ends.

### 5.6 Greater Body Transformation

**Factor:** Greater Body Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Major form change.

Default effect:

- choose full form template;
- record AC, temporary/form HP, Speed, movement modes, size, senses, speech, hands, equipment, attacks, traits, sphere-use limits, and cleanup;
- duration 1 minute;
- unwilling target saves;
- if form HP is used, damage beyond form HP carries to original HP unless Art says otherwise;
- on end, target reverts and may suffer Reversion Shock if form was broken.

### 5.7 Size Transformation

**Factor:** Size Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Changes size one category.

Default effect:

- willing target or object;
- unwilling target makes Constitution save;
- one size step up or down;
- record space, reach, carrying, weapon/armor interaction, squeezing, and damage changes if any;
- default does not change damage dice unless Art says so;
- duration 1 minute.

### 5.9 Movement Transformation

**Factor:** Movement Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Changes movement.

Default effect:

- choose one movement mode: climb, swim, burrow through soft material, glide, wall-walk, water-walk, cloud-step, shadow-step, source-supported movement;
- target gains movement equal to half Speed or PB × 10 feet;
- duration 1 minute;
- unwilling target resists if movement mode restricts or distorts them.

### 5.10 Flight Transformation

**Factor:** Flight Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Grants flight or wing/air-body form.

Default effect:

- willing target gains fly Speed equal to Speed for 1 minute;
- if knocked prone, restrained, incapacitated, or Transformation Layer suppressed, target falls unless hover is paid;
- hover requires source support or additional cost;
- unwilling target cannot be given unsafe flight/fall without save and source support.

### 5.11 Damage Type Transformation

**Factor:** Damage Type Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Changes damage expression.

Default effect:

- choose one damage packet or ongoing damage source;
- change to one source-supported damage type;
- duration one packet or 1 minute for ongoing effect;
- resistance/immunity applies to new type;
- on Transformation Check success by 5+, ignore one minor resistance only if source supports and paid by separate breach effect.

### 5.12 Object Reshaping

**Factor:** Object Reshaping  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Changes object shape.

Default effect:

- unattended object up to Medium or source size;
- attended object allows holder save;
- shape changes but material and mass remain similar;
- function must be recorded;
- cannot create complex machinery or magical function without Complex/Magical Function from Creation or equivalent source;
- duration 1 minute or 1 hour ritual.

### 5.13 Deep Object Reshaping

**Factor:** Deep Object Reshaping  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Changes object function or structure.

Default effect:

- Transformation Check against Break DC/material DC;
- on success, object gains one new function or loses one function for duration;
- on success by 5+, function is stable for 1 hour;
- on failure by 5+, object cracks, jams, or becomes unstable.

### 5.14 Effect Reshaping

**Factor:** Effect Reshaping  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Changes ongoing effect expression.

Default effect:

- choose ongoing effect you control or can contest;
- make Transformation Check against effect DC/controller DC;
- on success, change one parameter: damage type, area shape, visual form, movement direction, trigger condition, target category, or rider expression if source supports;
- on success by 5+, preserve duration without loss;
- on failure, effect remains unchanged;
- on failure by 5+, effect destabilizes or ends if source supports.

### 5.15 Condition Transformation

**Factor:** Condition Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Changes a condition into another state.

Default effect:

- choose one condition, curse symptom, poison state, disease symptom, Deviation symptom, Hidden Injury symptom, or Root Harm expression the source can touch;
- make Transformation Check against condition DC;
- on success, convert it into a less harmful, more stable, or different written condition for duration;
- on success by 5+, convert into stable Burden/treatment route if source supports;
- on failure, no change;
- on failure by 5+, condition worsens or mutates.

This does not heal by itself unless paired with Restoration/Soul Repair/Life.

### 5.16 Created Manifestation Upgrade

**Factor:** Created Manifestation Upgrade  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Transforms a created subject.

Default effect:

- choose Created Subject;
- make Transformation Check against Creation DC/Break DC;
- on success, add one Form Statistic, durability increase, movement mode, material trait, or source-supported function;
- on success by 5+, upgrade persists for created subject duration;
- on failure, no upgrade;
- on failure by 5+, created subject becomes unstable.

### 5.18 Offensive Form

**Factor:** Offensive Form  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Adds attack or harmful rider.

Default effect:

- transformed subject gains one listed attack or damage aura;
- attack uses source attack/save;
- damage one Form Package or source package;
- trigger frequency once per round;
- hostile targets save/AC normally.

### 5.19 Stable Transformation

**Factor:** Stable Transformation  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Stabilizes form.

Default effect:

- first successful Transformation Contest suppresses instead of ending the layer;
- duration increases one step;
- Reversion Shock reduced one step;
- unstable failure result downgraded once.

### 5.1 Tactical Coordination

**Factor:** Tactical Coordination  
**Mandate / CP:** +1 / +1 CP

Creates Tactical Order Layer.

Default effect:

- willing ally or subordinate;
- no save;
- target gains one bonus before start of your next turn: +PB to one attack/check/save, move 10 feet without provoking from one creature, draw/stow/use minor object, or gain one Command Die to a listed roll;
- target uses normal action economy unless effect says otherwise.

### 5.2 Coordinated Assault

**Factor:** Coordinated Assault  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates Coordinated Assault Layer.

Default effect:

- choose one enemy as Priority Mark;
- up to PB allies who can perceive command gain +PB or Command Die on first attack against marked target before start of your next turn;
- mark ends after PB qualifying attacks or duration end;
- target can remove mark by Command Contest or leaving communication/mark range if source requires.

### 5.3 Compel Simple Order

**Factor:** Compel Order  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Compelled Order Layer at Control Level 2.

Default simple orders:

- approach;
- retreat;
- drop held object;
- speak one short phrase;
- stay still;
- stand;
- kneel;
- look away;
- open hand;
- move up to half Speed;
- do not move;
- do not speak;
- do not take Reaction.

Target makes Command Save. On failure, obeys until start of caster's next turn. On success, no compulsion. On failed by 5+, order lasts until end of target's next turn.

### 5.4 Strong Compulsion

**Factor:** Strong Compulsion  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Raises hostile command to Control Level 3.

Default effect:

- target makes Command Save;
- on failure, target must use or lose one action category on its next turn;
- on failed by 5+, caster chooses between movement, Bonus Action, Reaction, or one weapon attack if legal;
- on success, target loses Reaction only if source supports pressure; otherwise no effect.

Full Action command requires Full Action Command gate or GM review.

### 5.5 Action Denial

**Factor:** Action Denial  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Action Denial Layer.

Default effect:

- choose one action category;
- target makes Command Save;
- on failure, target cannot use that category until start of caster's next turn;
- on success, target can use it but subtracts Command Die from first roll in that category;
- on failed by 5+, target also gains Priority Mark.

### 5.6 Broad Action Denial

**Factor:** Broad Action Denial  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Affects broader categories.

Default effect:

- choose two action categories or one broad set: attacks, techniques, movement, reactions/counters, item use, speech/commands;
- target saves;
- on failure, denied until start of caster's next turn;
- on success, deny one narrower subcategory only;
- GM review if it denies all Actions.

### 5.7 Subordinate Command

**Factor:** Subordinate Command  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Commands legal Subordinate Target.

Default effect:

- no save if target is willing/loyal/legal subordinate;
- if loyalty contested, make Command Check against morale/oath/authority DC;
- on success, target takes one Commanded Action within normal action economy;
- on success by 5+, order can be issued as Bonus Action;
- on failure, subordinate hesitates or requires its own action normally.

### 5.8 Command Override

**Factor:** Command Override  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Contests existing Command Layer.

Default effect:

- make Command Check against opposing Command DC;
- on success, suppress opposing command until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, replace it with one Tactical Order or Priority Mark;
- on success by 10+, break minor hostile command;
- on failure by 5+, opposing command marks you as challenger.

### 5.9 Rally Order

**Factor:** Rally Order  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Restores morale or recenters ally.

Default effect:

- choose willing ally or subordinate;
- target may immediately repeat one save against frightened, charmed, stunned-by-command, panic, confusion, demoralized, or command-pressure effect if source supports it;
- add Command Die or PB;
- on success, effect ends or suppresses until start of next turn;
- on failure, target gains temporary morale but condition remains.

### 5.10 Hierarchy Mark

**Factor:** Hierarchy Mark  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates Hierarchy Mark.

Default effect:

- mark one target as commander, subordinate, protected subject, oathbound, rebel, traitor, champion, officer, or unlawful actor;
- mark lasts 1 minute;
- while mark lasts, relevant Command Checks involving that hierarchy gain PB or Command Die;
- false mark can be contested by Command/Heaven/Revelation/Fate.

### 5.11 Command Voice

**Factor:** Command Medium  
**Mandate / CP:** +1 / +1 CP

Improves communication.

Default modes:

- audible voice reaches 60 feet;
- banner/gesture works through silence if visible;
- spiritual voice reaches creatures with spirit sense;
- formation signal reaches linked unit;
- talisman signal reaches marked target.

If communication is blocked, command fails unless medium bypasses that block.

### 5.12 Area Command

**Factor:** Area Command  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Command Area.

Default effect:

- area uses source dimensions or 20-foot radius;
- first time each round a legal target starts turn inside or enters, chosen Command Mode may apply;
- unwilling targets save separately;
- willing allies can receive Tactical Order once per round.

### 5.14 Group Command

**Factor:** Group Command  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Affects up to PB legal targets.

Default:

- same Order Mode applies to all targets;
- unwilling targets save separately;
- willing allies all receive same Tactical/Rally effect;
- command communication must reach all targets.

### 5.15 Immediate Commanded Movement

**Factor:** Immediate Commanded Movement  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Movement Order.

Default effect:

- willing target moves up to half Speed immediately using Reaction or no action if Art says;
- unwilling target saves; on failure, moves up to half Speed in a safe legal direction chosen by caster;
- cannot force movement into obvious lethal hazard;
- on failed save by 5+, movement does not provoke opportunity attacks from one creature chosen by caster if source supports tactical timing.

### 5.17 Commanded Attack

**Factor:** Commanded Attack  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates Commanded Attack.

Default effect:

- willing target uses Reaction or Bonus Action to make one weapon attack or simple listed attack;
- target chooses legal weapon/target unless Art specifies;
- unwilling target makes Command Save; on failure, makes one simple attack against a legal target chosen by caster if it does not violate Illegal Order Rule;
- on success, no attack;
- on failed by 5+, attack gains Command Die.

### 5.18 Commanded Sphere Use

**Factor:** Commanded Sphere Use  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Directs a named sphere effect, technique, item action, or manual technique.

Default effect:

- target must know/possess effect and have resources;
- willing/subordinate target may use effect with its normal action economy, or as Reaction if Art pays;
- unwilling target cannot be forced unless GM-reviewed and effect is simple/known/legal;
- target pays its own CP unless Art states caster pays;
- if resources unavailable, command fails without forcing payment.

### 5.19 Extended Command Duration

**Factor:** Extended Command Duration  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Extends one Command Layer.

Default:

- duration becomes 1 minute;
- target repeats save at end of each turn for hostile compulsion;
- Tactical/Rally marks persist until used or duration ends;
- repeated triggers are once per round.

### 5.21 Sect-Scale Command

**Factor:** Sect-Scale Command  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP, GM-reviewed

Commands a unit, squad, sect group, warband, formation crew, or retainer body.

Baseline:

- unit identity;
- authority source;
- communication medium;
- morale/authority DC;
- order type;
- duration;
- failure result;
- desertion/refusal route;
- collateral/social consequence.

### 5.1 Movement Increase

**Factor:** Movement Increase  
**Mandate / CP:** +1 / +1 CP

Default effect:

- willing target increases one movement mode by 10 feet × PB until start of next turn;
- or moves up to half Speed immediately if source supports burst movement;
- no save for willing target;
- counterplay: Slow, Binding, terrain, Domain Lock.

### 5.2 Short Teleport

**Factor:** Short Teleport  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Default effect:

- move self or willing target to visible legal destination within 30 feet or source range;
- Action or Bonus Action if source supports;
- arrival exact on success;
- if destination invalid, transport fails before target moves;
- unwilling target requires Forced Transport.

### 5.3 Long Teleport

**Factor:** Long Teleport  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default effect:

- destination must be Line-of-Sight, Known Location, Viewed Remotely, Anchor-Locked, or Marked Target;
- make Transport Check against distance/boundary DC if contested;
- on success, arrive exact or near;
- on failure, blocked or drift;
- on failure by 5+, Mishap.

### 5.4 True Teleport

**Factor:** True Teleport  
**Mandate / CP:** +6 / +6 CP

Default effect:

- may use Known Location, Viewed Remotely, Anchor-Locked, Paired Anchor, or Recall Point destination;
- ignores ordinary physical path but not Heaven, Domain, Binding, planar, anti-teleport, or destination illegality;
- requires Transport Check if destination is not currently visible;
- on success, exact or near arrival;
- on success by 5+, exact arrival;
- on failure, drift/blocked;
- on failure by 5+, Mishap.

### 5.5 Distance Increase I / II

**Factor:** Distance Increase  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP per step

Increase distance one step:

1. source range;
2. 30 feet;
3. 120 feet;
4. 1 mile;
5. same region;
6. same world;
7. cross-world / GM-reviewed.

Each step beyond same region requires stronger destination mode or Anchor.

### 5.6 Recall

**Factor:** Recall  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- designate Recall Point when Art is prepared or activated;
- duration 1 hour or scene;
- as Action or Reaction if trigger says, return willing target to Recall Point;
- if point blocked, arrive at nearest legal space within 10 × PB feet;
- if point destroyed, make Transport Check or suffer Mishap.

### 5.7 Forced Transport

**Factor:** Forced Transport  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- target makes Transport Save;
- on failure, move target up to 10 × PB feet to visible legal destination;
- on success, no movement or half distance if source supports shove;
- on failed by 5+, target loses Reaction or takes Transport Package;
- cannot move target into obviously lethal hazard without GM review/source support.

### 5.9 Ejection / Banish

**Factor:** Ejection  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Default effect:

- target makes Charisma or Wisdom save;
- on failure, eject from Domain, vehicle, possession space, pocket space, gate, threshold, spirit boundary, or source-supported area to nearest legal exterior point;
- on success, target remains but is pushed 5 × PB feet if source supports;
- if no legal exterior exists, effect fails or becomes Suppression.

### 5.10 Position Swap

**Factor:** Position Swap  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Default effect:

- choose two legal targets within range;
- willing targets swap with no save;
- unwilling target makes Transport Save;
- if either save succeeds, swap fails unless Art allows partial;
- on failed by 5+, unwilling target loses Reaction after swap;
- carried gear follows default carrying rule.

### 5.11 Path Opening

**Factor:** Path Opening  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Path Layer.

Default effect:

- create route through terrain, water, air, shadow, spirit, formation seam, domain boundary, wall seam, or source-supported obstacle;
- duration 1 minute;
- path requires movement to traverse;
- path has Path DC / Break DC equal to art save DC;
- hostile blocker can attempt Transport Contest;
- if path collapses while occupied, occupants move to nearest legal space or suffer Mishap if dangerous.

### 5.12 Stable Path

**Factor:** Stable Path  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Improves Path.

Default effect:

- path lasts 10 minutes or scene;
- travelers gain PB on checks to traverse;
- path resists first suppression attempt with +PB DC;
- collapse is harmless unless source says otherwise.

### 5.13 Open Gate

**Factor:** Open Gate  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates Gate Layer.

Default effect:

- create gate between origin and legal destination;
- duration 1 minute;
- crossing action: movement through gate;
- crossing frequency: one creature per round unless expanded;
- Gate Integrity = 5 × PB + 5 × Refinement Ability Modifier;
- Gate Break DC = art save DC;
- unauthorized travelers may be blocked by selection mode;
- if gate breaks, no further crossings; occupants in transit arrive nearest legal endpoint or suffer Mishap if hostile break.

### 5.14 Effect Transport

**Factor:** Effect Transport  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Moves an ongoing effect, mark, projectile, area origin, or created object effect.

Default effect:

- choose movable effect with legal source;
- make Transport Check against effect DC/creator DC/controller DC;
- on success, move effect origin up to source range or Transport distance;
- on success by 5+, preserve duration without loss;
- on failure, effect remains;
- on failure by 5+, effect destabilizes or ends if source supports.

Cannot move a Domain, Soul Vessel, or permanent effect without specific support.

### 5.15 Group Transport

**Factor:** Group Transport  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Affects up to PB willing targets.

Default effect:

- all targets must be within source range/origin area;
- same destination;
- each unwilling target requires Forced Transport;
- if destination lacks space, excess targets arrive nearest legal spaces or transport fails for them;
- carried gear follows carrying limit.

### 5.16 Mass Transport

**Factor:** Mass Transport  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP, GM-reviewed if huge

Default effect:

- affects group, vehicle, squad, or large object;
- requires Anchor or Gate for long distance;
- Transport Check against mass/route DC;
- on failure, partial movement or Mishap;
- must state carrying capacity and excluded subjects.

### 5.17 Emergency Transport

**Factor:** Emergency Transport  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Reaction transport.

Default triggers:

- target would be hit;
- target drops to 0 HP;
- target enters hazard;
- target is caught by area effect;
- target is sealed/banished;
- gate collapses.

Default effect:

- Reaction;
- transport target to safe legal point within short range;
- if unwilling, save applies;
- if trigger already resolved, cannot undo without Time/Fate/Soul support.

### 5.19 Planar / World Crossing

**Factor:** Planar Crossing  
**Mandate / CP:** +6 / +6 CP, GM-reviewed

Default effect:

- requires Boundary Crossing or Planar Destination Mode;
- destination must be Anchor-Locked, Paired Anchor, Gate, ritual coordinate, or GM-approved known crossing;
- Transport Check against boundary DC;
- on success, crossing occurs;
- on success by 5+, crossing is stable and safe;
- on failure, crossing fails or drift to boundary-adjacent location;
- on failure by 5+, Mishap plus boundary attention.

### 5.20 Safe Return Clause

**Factor:** Safe Return Clause  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates return fallback.

Default effect:

- designate fallback destination when transport occurs;
- if target would be stranded, gate closes, route collapses, or destination becomes illegal within duration, make Transport Check;
- on success, return to fallback;
- on failure, remain stranded or arrive nearest legal space;
- on failure by 5+, Mishap.

### 5.1 Mirror Defense

**Factor:** Mirror Defense  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates Mirror Defense Layer.

Default effect:

- Reaction when target is attacked or forced to save;
- add PB or one Reflection Die to AC/save before result is declared;
- on success by 5+ on Reflection Check, also apply Mirror Mark to attacker/source until start of next turn;
- one use.

### 5.2 Attack Reflection

**Factor:** Attack Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Reflects a weapon/ranged/melee/sphere attack.

Default effect:

- Reaction in Impact Window;
- make Reflection Check against attack roll total;
- on success, attack misses original target and is redirected to source or legal target within original range;
- original attack roll is used against new target AC;
- on success by 5+, add one Reflection Package to damage if hit or choose third target;
- on failure, attack resolves normally.

### 5.3 Effect Reflection

**Factor:** Effect Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Reflects single-target save/check effect.

Default effect:

- Reaction when a single-target effect targets protected creature;
- make Reflection Check against effect DC;
- on success, original target is protected and effect redirects to source or legal target;
- redirected target makes original save against original DC;
- on success by 5+, source has Disadvantage or subtracts Reflection Die from save;
- on failure, original effect resolves normally.

### 5.6 Condition Reflection

**Factor:** Condition Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Reflects one condition.

Default effect:

- when target would receive a condition from a reflectable effect, make Reflection Check against effect DC;
- on success, original target ignores condition and source/redirected target saves against same condition;
- on success by 5+, reflected target has Disadvantage on its save;
- on failure, original condition applies.

Cannot reflect conditions from environmental facts unless source supports it.

### 5.7 Movement Reflection

**Factor:** Movement Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Reflects forced movement.

Default effect:

- Reaction when target would be pushed, pulled, teleported, knocked prone by movement, or displaced;
- make Reflection Check against source DC;
- on success, original movement is negated and source/redirected target is moved the same distance/direction if legal;
- on success by 5+, choose direction among legal reflected options;
- on failure, movement occurs.

Transport/Binding sources may contest.

### 5.8 Beneficial Reflection

**Factor:** Beneficial Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Mirrors a beneficial effect.

Default effect:

- when a willing target receives a beneficial single-target effect, choose one additional legal target within range;
- pay mirrored CP if source effect has CP cost unless Art uses stored charge;
- mirrored target receives reduced version: half duration, one die less, or PB-limited bonus;
- on Reflection Check success by 5+, mirrored benefit equals original minor effect;
- does not stack with same source unless allowed.

### 5.9 Effect Echo

**Factor:** Effect Echo  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates Echoed Effect.

Default effect:

- choose one known/observed/recorded effect with defined action surface;
- make Reflection Check against effect DC;
- on success, create one echo at half duration or one package weaker;
- on success by 5+, echo uses full minor effect;
- on failure, no echo;
- echo cannot copy unknown resources, hidden riders, or undefined enemy techniques.

### 5.10 Ongoing Effect Reflection

**Factor:** Ongoing Effect Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Reflects or redirects ongoing effect.

Default effect:

- choose one ongoing effect currently affecting target;
- make Reflection Check against effect DC/controller DC;
- on success, suppress on original target and apply reduced copy to source/redirected target until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, transfer full remaining duration up to 1 minute;
- on failure, effect remains.

### 5.11 Counter-Reflection

**Factor:** Counter-Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Counters another Reflection Layer.

Default effect:

- Reaction when Reflection would occur;
- make Reflection Check against opposing Reflection DC;
- on success, suppress reflection and original effect proceeds;
- on success by 5+, rebound backlash to reflector;
- on failure, opponent reflection proceeds.

### 5.12 Redirect to Third Target

**Factor:** Redirect to Third Target  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Allows third target.

Default effect:

- reflected attack/effect may target a legal third target within original range or Reflection range;
- third target must satisfy target legality;
- unwilling third target receives original save/defense;
- if no legal third target, reflection defaults to source or fails.

### 5.14 Area Edge Reflection

**Factor:** Area Edge Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Reflects area edge.

Default effect:

- protect one target in area or on edge;
- reduce area damage by one Reflection Package;
- if reduced to 0, redirect one ray/line/edge segment or create safe pocket until start of next turn;
- full area reversal requires GM review and explicit area size.

### 5.15 Group Reflection

**Factor:** Group Reflection  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Affects up to PB protected targets.

Default effect:

- same Reflection Mode applies to group;
- each trigger consumes one use or uses field frequency;
- Reaction can protect one target; field can protect multiple if paid;
- no target can benefit more than once per round.

### 5.16 Sustained Mirror Field

**Factor:** Sustained Mirror Field  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates Mirror Field.

Default effect:

- area 10-foot radius or source area;
- duration 1 minute with maintenance if source requires;
- first reflectable attack/effect against a protected target in field each round triggers Mirror Defense or Damage Rebound;
- field has Reflection DC and can be suppressed by Reflection Contest.

### 5.17 Persistent Mirror Mark

**Factor:** Persistent Mirror Mark  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Mirror Mark.

Default effect:

- mark lasts 1 minute;
- next reflectable trigger against marked target activates chosen Reflection Mode;
- mark ends after trigger unless persistent duration paid;
- mark can be removed by Reflection Contest, Revelation, Concealment, or source counter.

### 5.1 Entropy Pressure

**Factor:** Entropy Pressure  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates Entropy Pressure Layer.

Default effect:

- choose one Decay Mode;
- target makes Entropy Save if creature or controller resists;
- on failure, apply one Entropy Package or PB + Refinement Ability Modifier reduction;
- trigger frequency once per round;
- duration 1 minute;
- on failed by 5+, advance Collapse Clock one stage.

### 5.3 Durability Decay

**Factor:** Durability Decay  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Damages object, barrier, ward, created subject, equipment, structure, vessel, anchor, or Domain Boundary.

Default effect:

- apply one Entropy Package to HP/Integrity;
- reduce Break DC bonus by PB if present;
- on reaching 0, subject breaks/collapses per its cleanup rules;
- attended object allows holder save.

### 5.4 Healing Decay

**Factor:** Healing Decay  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Reduces healing.

Default effect:

- first time each round target would regain HP, reduce healing by one Entropy Package;
- if reduced to 0, healing fails for that trigger;
- on failed save by 5+, target cannot regain HP until start of next turn;
- does not damage by itself unless Inversion of Recovery is used.

### 5.8 Duration Erosion

**Factor:** Duration Erosion  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Reduces duration.

Default effect:

- choose one ongoing effect with duration;
- make Entropy Check against effect DC;
- on success, reduce duration one Duration Step;
- on success by 5+, reduce two minor steps or one major step;
- if reduced below 1 round, effect ends at start of next turn;
- on failure, no change.

### 5.10 Resource Leakage

**Factor:** Resource Leakage  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Leaks non-CP resources.

Default effect:

- choose charges, uses, stored dice, ammunition, medicine doses, talisman charges, formation fuel, resource units, item charges, or stored effect count;
- target/controller makes Entropy Save or Check;
- on failure, lose one unit or PB units for minor resources;
- on failed by 5+, also increase next use cost by 1 unit if possible.

### 5.11 CP Leakage

**Factor:** CP Leakage  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Leaks CP or equivalent Path resource.

Default effect:

- target makes Constitution/Charisma/Wisdom save based on Path/source;
- on failure, lose CP equal to PB + Refinement Ability Modifier, minimum PB;
- on success, lose half or none for protected targets;
- on failed by 5+, next CP cost before start of next turn increases by PB;
- cannot reduce below 0.

### 5.12 Pressure Leakage

**Factor:** Pressure Leakage  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Increases maintenance/cost pressure.

Default effect:

- choose one cost type: CP upkeep, concentration/maintenance check, item charge, Domain upkeep, formation fuel, healing cost, repair cost, movement cost, command cost;
- next time cost is paid within duration, increase by PB or one unit;
- if target cannot pay, effect suppresses until start of next turn;
- on failed by 5+, cost increase applies twice.

### 5.13 Function Decay

**Factor:** Function Decay  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Suppresses function.

Default effect:

- choose one function: flight, speech, hand use, weapon property, armor property, item action, gate crossing, shield layer, reaction feature, movement mode, detection mode, healing mode, created subject function;
- target/controller saves;
- on failure, function suppresses until start of next turn;
- on failed by 5+, suppress until end of next turn;
- on success, function works but takes one Entropy Package durability/resource pressure if applicable.

### 5.14 Condition Worsening

**Factor:** Condition Worsening  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Worsens an existing condition.

Default effect:

- choose one existing poison, disease, curse, fatigue, Deviation symptom, Hidden Injury symptom, Soul Wound, max HP pressure, corrosion, burning, freezing, exhaustion-like strain, or unstable condition;
- target makes Entropy Save;
- on failure, advance severity one stage or increase DC by PB until next treatment;
- on failed by 5+, add one linked symptom or Collapse Clock stage;
- Restoration/Soul Repair/Life can contest.

### 5.15 Stability Decay

**Factor:** Stability Decay  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Attacks stabilization.

Default effect:

- choose stabilized condition, ongoing treatment, Soul Mooring, Fortification Layer, Domain Layer, Transformation Layer, Creation Layer, seal, formation, or ritual maintenance;
- make Entropy Check against layer DC;
- on success, remove one stability benefit, reduce duration, or force maintenance check;
- on success by 5+, suppress layer until start of next turn.

### 5.16 Collapse Clock

**Factor:** Collapse Clock  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates clock.

Default effect:

- choose target and Collapse Condition;
- clock starts at 0 and fills on triggers;
- minor target collapses at 2, durable at 3, major at 5;
- trigger frequency once per round;
- target/controller may attempt Entropy Save each trigger;
- failure advances clock 1; failure by 5+ advances 2; success prevents advance;
- when full, Collapse Condition resolves.

### 5.17 Anti-Restoration Entropy

**Factor:** Anti-Restoration Entropy  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Counters recovery effects.

Default effect:

- Reaction or prepared layer when target receives healing, repair, restoration, fortification, purification, stabilization, duration extension, or mark removal;
- make Entropy Check against recovery effect DC;
- on success, reduce recovery by one Entropy Package;
- on success by 5+, if recovery reduced to 0, suppress recovery source until start of next turn;
- on failure, recovery proceeds.

### 5.18 Inversion of Recovery

**Factor:** Inversion of Recovery  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Converts failed recovery into harm.

Default effect:

- requires Anti-Restoration Entropy;
- if recovery is reduced to 0 by Entropy, target makes Entropy Save;
- on failure, take one Entropy Package damage, CP loss, or condition worsening;
- on success, no inversion harm;
- GM review for lethal inversion loops.

### 5.19 Inevitable Decline

**Factor:** Inevitable Decline  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Signature entropy.

Default effect:

- choose one decline category: healing, repair, defense, duration, resource, movement, action maintenance, creation durability, domain integrity, transformation stability;
- first time each round target uses or benefits from that category, Entropy Pressure applies automatically;
- target saves each trigger;
- duration 1 minute;
- on three failed saves, Collapse Clock stage triggers or major suppression occurs;
- counterplay requires Entropy Contest or category-specific treatment.

### 5.1 Omen Reading

**Factor:** Omen Reading  
**Mandate / CP:** +1 / +1 CP

Creates an Omen Layer.

Default effect:

- Action;
- ask one narrow question about danger, trigger, likely route, hidden cost, or near-future event;
- make Fate Check against relevant DC;
- on success, learn one Omen Fact;
- on success by 5+, learn one safe/unsafe branch;
- on success by 10+, learn one countermeasure or avoided trigger;
- on failure, no clear omen;
- on failure by 5+, false omen or Fate Backlash.

Omen does not replace Revelation. It predicts likely pressure, not hidden full mechanics.

### 5.2 Fate Mark

**Factor:** Fate Mark  
**Mandate / CP:** +1 / +1 CP

Creates a Fate Mark.

Default effect:

- Action or part of another Fate effect;
- target makes Fate Save if unwilling;
- on failure, mark attaches for 1 minute;
- on success, mark fails or lasts until start of your next turn;
- mark allows one future Fate Layer to target or trigger against the target;
- mark can be removed by Fate Contest, curse removal, Heaven/Soul protection, or trigger expiration.

Mark Modes:

- Fortune Mark;
- Doom Mark;
- Prophecy Mark;
- Arrival Mark;
- Survival Mark;
- Debt Mark;
- Severance Mark.

### 5.3 Fortune Thread

**Factor:** Fortune Thread  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates a Fortune Thread.

Default effect:

- choose one legal target and one roll category: attack, save, check, damage/healing package, Break Attempt, contest, or treatment check;
- duration 1 minute or until used;
- once before expiration, target may add one Fate Die to the chosen roll;
- target chooses after rolling but before result is declared;
- if unused, thread fades.

Success by 5+ on creation grants one additional eligible roll category or extends duration to scene.

### 5.4 Doom Thread

**Factor:** Doom Thread  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates a Doom Thread.

Default effect:

- unwilling target makes Fate Save;
- on failure, choose one roll category;
- once before duration ends, when target makes that roll, subtract one Fate Die;
- on failed save by 5+, target also gains visible Fate Mark until end of scene;
- on successful save, thread fails.

Doom Thread cannot force failure of a roll that has no legal chance to fail.

### 5.6 Chosen Branch

**Factor:** Chosen Branch  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates a Branch Layer.

Default effect:

- define Branch Set of two legal outcomes before the triggering roll/event resolves;
- when trigger occurs, caster chooses one branch if it remains legal;
- if chosen branch is illegal when triggered, no branch is chosen and Fate Layer fades;
- unwilling affected targets may receive Fate Save if branch harms them.

Example branches:

- "the attack strikes shield instead of body";
- "the fall lands in the river instead of stone";
- "the gate opens loudly instead of silently";
- "the target drops the item instead of being knocked prone";
- "the poison reveals itself now instead of later."

### 5.7 Reroll Fate

**Factor:** Reroll Fate  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Reroll Layer.

Default effect:

- Reaction after a legal d20 roll is made and before final outcome is declared;
- force or allow one reroll;
- if target is unwilling, it makes Fate Save;
- new roll must be used unless the Art states better control;
- once used, layer ends.

No roll can be rerolled more than once by the same Fate Art.

### 5.8 Fate Lock

**Factor:** Fate Lock  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Fate Lock.

Default effect:

- choose one active Fate Layer, mark, prophecy trigger, declared Branch, oath condition, or legal future condition;
- duration 1 minute;
- attempts to remove, alter, hide, or invalidate it require Fate Contest against Fate DC;
- on failed contest, lock remains;
- on success, lock suppresses until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, lock breaks.

Fate Lock cannot make an invalid prophecy valid.

### 5.9 Karmic Convergence

**Factor:** Karmic Convergence  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Convergence Thread.

Default effect:

- choose two legally linked subjects with Karmic Link;
- duration 1 minute;
- once per round when one subject moves, targets, attacks, flees, searches, or triggers a relevant effect, Fate may pull the event toward the other subject if legal;
- make Fate Check against opposing DC if resisted;
- on success, reduce distance by up to PB × 5 feet, reveal direction, redirect a search clue, or make a legal path present;
- on success by 5+, also apply Fate Mark;
- on failure, no convergence that round.

Convergence cannot teleport unless Transport is also used.

### 5.10 Coincidence

**Factor:** Coincidence  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates a Coincidence Layer.

Default effect:

- declare one plausible minor coincidence within the scene;
- make Fate Check against GM-set scene DC or opposing Fate/Domain/Heaven DC;
- on success, coincidence occurs;
- on success by 5+, it occurs with favorable timing;
- on failure, no coincidence;
- on failure by 5+, coincidence favors opposition or Fate Backlash triggers.

Coincidence Categories:

1. an unattended mundane object is present;
2. a door is unlocked but not unguarded;
3. weather shifts one step if weather is plausible;
4. a bystander looks away;
5. a dropped item lands within reach;
6. a message arrives at awkward timing;
7. a legal route is available but costly;
8. a weak witness remembers one useful detail;
9. a formation has one overlooked maintenance seam;
10. an enemy's boast reveals a narrow clue.

Coincidence cannot create rare treasure, erase enemies, force surrender, or make impossible facts true.

### 5.11 Foretold Survival

**Factor:** Foretold Survival  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Survival Thread.

Default effect:

- choose one target and one survival trigger: drop to 0 HP, fail a save, suffer lethal damage, fail a tribulation wave, fail a Breakthrough-related trial, be sealed, be banished, or be cut off from recovery;
- duration 1 minute or scene for ritual prophecy;
- when trigger occurs, target makes Fate Check or Fate Save as appropriate;
- on success, convert result into survival with severe cost;
- on success by 5+, reduce the cost one step;
- on failure, normal consequence occurs;
- on failure by 5+, Fate Backlash or worsened consequence.

Default severe costs:

- target drops to 1 HP instead of 0 but gains a Hidden Injury/Strain mark;
- target is not killed but is unconscious and marked;
- target avoids banishment but loses Reaction and CP equal to PB;
- target survives tribulation strike but gains omen scar;
- target remains reachable for rescue but cannot act until next turn.

Foretold Survival cannot be chained with itself in the same scene unless GM-approved.

### 5.12 Foretold Doom

**Factor:** Foretold Doom  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Doomed End Thread.

Default effect:

- choose one target, one doom trigger, and one consequence;
- target makes Fate Save;
- on failure, doom attaches for 1 minute;
- when trigger occurs, consequence applies;
- on failed save by 5+, consequence also gains one Fate Die;
- on successful save, doom fails.

Default consequences:

- next qualifying attack gains Fate Die to damage or hit;
- target's next save against named effect subtracts Fate Die;
- target cannot regain HP until start of next turn after trigger;
- target's false layer drops for 1 round;
- target is pulled into legal range of linked consequence;
- target's escape route closes if already plausible.

Foretold Doom cannot declare unavoidable death.

### 5.13 Thread Transfer

**Factor:** Thread Transfer  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Moves a Fate Layer between legal targets.

Default effect:

- Action;
- choose one Fate Layer you can perceive;
- choose legal recipient connected by Karmic Link, shared scene, oath, bloodline, mark, attack, or source route;
- unwilling recipient makes Fate Save;
- on failure, Fate Layer transfers;
- on success, transfer fails;
- on failure by 5+, transferred layer duration extends 1 round;
- source target loses the layer unless Factor says copy.

Cannot transfer a Fate Layer to an illegal or immune target.

### 5.14 Thread Cutting

**Factor:** Thread Cutting  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Cuts or suppresses one Fate Thread.

Default effect:

- Action;
- make Fate Check against Fate DC of target Thread;
- on success, suppress Thread until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, remove minor Thread;
- on success by 10+, remove major Thread if not protected by Fate Lock/Heaven/Soul/Domain authority;
- on failure, Thread remains;
- on failure by 5+, caster receives Doom Thread until end of next turn.

### 5.15 Prophecy Seed

**Factor:** Prophecy Seed  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Prophecy Thread.

Default effect:

- write or speak trigger and consequence;
- duration scene or GM-approved ritual interval;
- target may receive Fate Save if prophecy harms it;
- if trigger occurs, consequence resolves using written mechanics;
- if trigger never occurs, prophecy expires;
- if trigger is deliberately made impossible by caster after creation, Fate Backlash may trigger.

Prophecy consequence must be one of:

- apply Fortune Thread;
- apply Doom Thread;
- apply Fate Mark;
- apply Omen Fact;
- trigger Sanction-like source consequence if source supports it;
- open/close a plausible route;
- reveal a Countermeasure Fact;
- create a Coincidence;
- trigger Foretold Survival/Doom if those Factors are included.

### 5.16 Destined Arrival

**Factor:** Destined Arrival  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates an Arrival Thread.

Default effect:

- choose legal destination, person, object, scene, clue, gate, or meeting point;
- make Fate Check against scene/route/opposition DC;
- on success, learn the next step toward arrival or make one plausible route available;
- on success by 5+, reduce travel/search complication by one step;
- on success by 10+, arrive at dramatically favorable timing if already plausible;
- on failure, no route opens;
- on failure by 5+, arrive late, with complication, or at cost.

Destined Arrival does not teleport without Transport.

### 5.17 Ongoing Fate

**Factor:** Ongoing Fate  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Extends one Fate Layer.

Default effect:

- duration becomes 10 minutes or until scene end if noncombat;
- trigger frequency remains once per round;
- each trigger after the first costs 1 CP unless Art uses Install-Paid or stored charge;
- if upkeep is not paid, layer suppresses until next turn.

### 5.18 Group Fate

**Factor:** Group Fate  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Affects legal targets up to Proficiency Bonus.

Default effect:

- choose targets at creation;
- each target receives same Thread Type;
- each unwilling target saves separately;
- Fortune/Doom dice are separate but still do not stack on same roll from same caster.

### 5.20 Scene Fate

**Factor:** Scene Fate  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP, GM-reviewed

Applies Fate pressure to the whole encounter scene.

Default effect:

- choose one Thread Type or Omen structure;
- trigger frequency once per round total;
- GM review required;
- all affected targets must have legal trigger and save/check;
- scene layer has Fate DC and contest route.

### 5.3 Initiative Command

**Factor:** Initiative Command  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates an Initiative Layer.

Default effect:

- Action at start of combat, start of round, or as Reaction when initiative is rolled if Art allows;
- choose one target;
- make Time Check against target initiative result or Time DC;
- on success, move target initiative up or down by PB places, or add/subtract Time Die to initiative;
- on success by 5+, choose exact position within legal round segment;
- on failure, no change;
- on failure by 5+, caster loses Reaction or gains Causality Debt.

Cannot give a creature two turns in one round unless Extra Turn is used.

### 5.4 Duration Command

**Factor:** Duration Command  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Duration Layer.

Default effect:

- choose one effect with duration;
- make Time Check against effect DC/creator DC/controller DC;
- on success, move duration one Duration Step up or down;
- on success by 5+, move two minor steps or one major step;
- on failure, no change;
- on failure by 5+, duration shifts unfavorably one minor step.

Cannot make instantaneous effects ongoing unless Store Effect/Repeat Moment supports it.

### 5.5 Delay Effect

**Factor:** Delay Effect  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Delay Layer.

Default effect:

- Reaction when a legal effect would resolve, or Action to prepare delay;
- make Time Check against effect DC or target save;
- on success, delay resolution until start or end of next turn;
- on success by 5+, delay up to 1 round;
- on failure, effect resolves normally;
- on failure by 5+, caster suffers Causality Debt.

Delayed effect keeps its original targets unless they become illegal; if illegal, effect fizzles or resolves at last legal position as source supports.

### 5.6 Store Effect

**Factor:** Store Effect  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Stored Moment.

Default effect:

- choose one legal effect at casting or while resolving;
- pay CP and create Temporal Mark;
- stored effect may be released once before duration ends;
- release uses the stored effect's original action or Reaction unless Art pays for easier release;
- if not released, stored effect expires;
- storage duration 1 minute by default;
- stored effect can be removed by Time Contest or breaking Temporal Mark.

Stored effect cannot be duplicated unless Repeat Moment is added.

### 5.7 Repeat Moment

**Factor:** Repeat Moment  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Repeat Layer.

Default effect:

- choose one legal roll, movement segment, damage instance, healing instance, or minor effect that just resolved;
- make Time Check against original DC or source DC;
- on success, repeat the same effect once against same target/area if still legal;
- on success by 5+, may choose a new legal target within same targeting rules;
- on failure, no repeat;
- on failure by 5+, Causality Debt.

Repeat Moment cannot repeat Extra Turn, Time Stop Field, or another Repeat Moment.

### 5.8 Rewind Roll

**Factor:** Rewind Roll  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Roll Rewind Layer.

Default effect:

- Reaction after one d20 roll but before final consequence is applied;
- make Time Check against roll DC or source DC if target unwilling;
- on success, reroll the d20;
- new roll is used unless Art includes Chosen Branch/Fate support;
- on success by 5+, add or subtract one Time Die after reroll;
- on failure, original roll stands;
- on failure by 5+, caster loses Reaction next round or gains Causality Debt.

A roll can be rewound once.

### 5.9 Rewind State

**Factor:** Rewind State  
**Mandate / CP:** +6 / +6 CP

Creates a Timeline Snapshot and Rewind Layer.

Default effect:

- Action to create Snapshot of one target's narrow state;
- Snapshot duration 1 minute;
- Reaction or Action to restore one recorded state if trigger occurs;
- allowed states: position, current HP within one Time Package, condition presence, duration remaining, broken/unbroken object state, spent/unspent reaction, or one named mark;
- on restore, pay Causality Debt;
- unwilling target receives Time Save;
- on success by 5+, reduce Causality Debt one step;
- on failure, restore fails.

Cannot restore death, lost soul, expended major resource, full turn, or campaign state unless GM-reviewed and supported by Soul/Heaven/Fate.

### 5.10 Temporal Stasis

**Factor:** Temporal Stasis  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Creates a Stasis Layer.

Default effect:

- target makes Time Save;
- on failure, target enters stasis until start of caster's next turn;
- while in stasis: cannot act, move, speak, use reactions, spend CP, or be moved by mundane means;
- durations on target do not tick unless Art says external time still affects them;
- target has Resistance to damage from outside stasis unless Art says it is fully isolated;
- on successful save, target is slowed until start of next turn instead;
- on failed save by 5+, stasis lasts until end of caster's next turn.

Counterplay: Time Contest, Heaven/Domain authority, breaking stasis anchor, damage if stasis is fragile.

### 5.11 Borrowed Action

**Factor:** Borrowed Action  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Borrowed Action Layer.

Default effect:

- willing target only unless Stolen Action is used;
- target immediately takes one listed action category: movement, Bonus Action, Reaction, object interaction, or one weapon attack;
- target incurs Causality Debt;
- next time target would use that category before end of next turn, it cannot;
- if category never comes due, target loses Reaction or Speed next turn.

Cannot borrow full Action unless Extra Action Window is used.

### 5.12 Stolen Action

**Factor:** Stolen Action  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Stolen Action Layer.

Default effect:

- target makes Time Save;
- on failure, choose one action category: Reaction, Bonus Action, movement, object interaction, or one attack;
- target loses that category until start of next turn;
- on failed save by 5+, caster or chosen ally may immediately take a related minor window: move 10 feet, make one object interaction, or gain one Reaction;
- on success, no theft;
- on success by 5+, target is immune to this Art until end of scene.

Stealing a full Action requires Extra Action Window or GM review.

### 5.13 Extra Action Window

**Factor:** Extra Action Window  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Creates an Extra Action Window.

Default effect:

- willing target gains one extra limited Action before end of current turn;
- allowed actions: Dash, Disengage, Dodge, Help, Hide, Use an Object, make one weapon attack, activate one named low-complexity technique, or another listed action;
- cannot cast/use another Time Art from this extra window;
- after using it, target gains Causality Debt;
- once per scene per target by default unless GM-approved.

### 5.14 Extra Turn

**Factor:** Extra Turn  
**Mandate / CP:** +8 / +8 CP

Creates an Extra Turn Layer.

Default effect:

- willing target takes one extra turn immediately after current turn or at end of round;
- extra turn includes movement, Action, Bonus Action, and Reaction refresh only if Art specifies; default refreshes movement and Action only;
- cannot use Time Art during extra turn;
- cannot gain another extra turn this scene from same source;
- after extra turn, target suffers Causality Debt and loses Reaction until start of next normal turn;
- GM review recommended.

Unwilling target cannot be granted extra turn as harm without Command/Fate/Heaven justification.

### 5.15 Time Stop Field

**Factor:** Time Stop Field  
**Mandate / CP:** +10 / +10 CP

Creates a Time Stop Field.

GM-reviewed by default, but uses this chassis.

Default effect:

- area: 10-foot radius or personal field;
- duration: one Moment, ending after caster takes one listed non-hostile action;
- frozen subjects cannot act, move, react, or perceive normally;
- caster cannot directly damage or apply hostile effects to frozen subjects during the stopped Moment unless the Art pays for hostile resolution;
- objects can be moved only if unattended and within carrying capacity;
- delayed hostile effects resolve when field ends;
- no Time Art can be cast within the stopped Moment;
- after field ends, caster gains Causality Debt.

Hostile Time Stop requires GM review, clear target saves, and severe cost.

### 5.16 Temporal Anchor

**Factor:** Temporal Anchor  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates a Temporal Anchor.

Default effect:

- choose one target, location, effect, or object;
- duration 1 minute;
- target gains Advantage or Time Die against forced temporal movement, rewind, delay, stasis, slow, stolen action, or duration reduction;
- first hostile Time effect against anchored target must beat Anchor Time DC or fail;
- anchor can be broken by Time Contest or Break Attempt.

### 5.17 Temporal Severance

**Factor:** Temporal Severance  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Cuts a Time Layer or temporal connection.

Default effect:

- Action;
- choose one active Time Layer, Temporal Mark, Stored Moment, Stasis, Delay, Duration Layer, or Snapshot;
- make Time Check against Time DC;
- on success, suppress until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, remove minor layer;
- on success by 10+, remove major layer if not protected;
- on failure by 5+, caster gains Causality Debt.

### 5.19 Group Time

**Factor:** Group Time  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Affects legal targets up to Proficiency Bonus.

Default effect:

- same Time Mode applies to each target;
- each unwilling target saves separately;
- trigger frequency once per target;
- action-economy grants cannot exceed one extra category per target.

### 5.21 Scene Time

**Factor:** Scene Time  
**Mandate / CP:** +7 / +7 CP, GM-reviewed

Affects whole encounter scene.

Default effect:

- choose one Time Mode;
- trigger frequency once per round total or once per target if GM approves;
- all targets get save/check as applicable;
- layer can be contested by Time Contest or Heaven/Domain authority.

### 5.1 Soul Strike

**Factor:** Soul Strike  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates a Soul Damage Layer.

Default effect:

- target makes Soul Save or is hit by source attack;
- on failure/hit, takes one Soul Package;
- on successful save, half damage;
- on failed save by 5+, apply minor Soul Wound if Art includes Soul Wound;
- counterplay: Soul Shield, Protection, Heaven, Soul Contest.

### 5.2 Max HP Pressure

**Factor:** Max HP Pressure  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Max HP Pressure Layer.

Default effect:

- target makes Constitution or Charisma Soul Save;
- on failure, reduce max HP by one Soul Package or PB + Refinement Ability Modifier;
- on success, no reduction or reduction lasts until start of next turn;
- on failed by 5+, reduction lasts until legal treatment or long rest;
- cannot reduce below half maximum without GM review.

### 5.3 Soul Wound

**Factor:** Soul Wound  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates a Soul Wound Layer.

Default effect:

- requires Soul Strike, Max HP Pressure, possession damage, severance, curse, or Root Harm source;
- target makes Soul Save;
- on failure, apply one minor Soul Wound symptom;
- on failed by 5+, symptom becomes major or two minor symptoms;
- on success, no persistent wound;
- treatment route must be recorded.

### 5.4 Soul Shield

**Factor:** Soul Shield  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Creates Soul Shield Layer.

Default effect:

- target gains Shield Integrity equal to one Soul Package;
- lasts 1 minute;
- when a protected soul-layer attack occurs, reduce incoming Soul Package or add PB to Soul Save;
- each use consumes Integrity equal to damage prevented or PB;
- at 0 Integrity, shield ends;
- success by 5+ on creation adds +PB Integrity.

### 5.5 Soul Mooring

**Factor:** Soul Mooring  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates Soul Mooring Layer.

Default effect:

- lasts 1 minute or until triggered;
- when target would be severed, dispersed, possessed, displaced, transferred, or become unreachable, make Soul Check;
- on success, target remains stable/reachable until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, also repair or reinforce one Soul Tether by PB;
- on failure, reveal threat route;
- on failure by 5+, mooring breaks and target gains Soul Wound/complication if source supports it.

### 5.6 Soul Vessel

**Factor:** Soul Vessel  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates or empowers Soul Vessel Layer.

Default effect:

- create vessel or designate legal vessel;
- choose capacity: memory mark, soul trace, spirit echo, companion remnant, possession link, soul fragment, or disembodied self;
- vessel uses default AC/Integrity/Break DC;
- unwilling occupant receives Soul Save;
- break result must be one of: release, return, disperse, backlash, seal, or remain as trace;
- vessel grants no action capacity unless paid.

### 5.7 Possession

**Factor:** Possession  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates Possession Link.

Default effect:

- target makes Wisdom or Charisma Soul Save;
- on failure, create Possession Link at Level 1 Influence for 1 minute;
- on failed by 5+, Level 2 Ride;
- Level 3+ requires stronger Art or repeated success;
- host repeats save at end of each turn if control affects action category;
- possession cannot force obvious self-destruction without GM review;
- exorcism and Soul Contest can suppress/break link.

### 5.8 Exorcism

**Factor:** Exorcism  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Suppresses or breaks Possession Link.

Default effect:

- make Soul Check against Possession DC;
- on success, suppress link until start of possessor's next turn;
- on success by 5+, reduce control level by 1 or eject Level 1/2 link;
- on success by 10+, eject major link if not protected;
- on failure, link remains;
- on failure by 5+, exorcist takes one Soul Package or gains possession vulnerability.

### 5.9 Soul Severance

**Factor:** Soul Severance  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Cuts a Soul Tether, Soul Mooring, Possession Link, Memory Mark, vessel connection, companion bond, or soul-body connection.

Default effect:

- make Soul Check against target Soul DC;
- unwilling target or controller may force Soul Save;
- on success, suppress connection until start of next turn;
- on success by 5+, sever minor connection or damage major connection by one stage;
- on success by 10+, sever major connection if not protected;
- on failure by 5+, caster suffers Soul Backlash.

### 5.10 Soul Repair

**Factor:** Soul Repair  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates Soul Repair Layer.

Default effect:

- choose one named Root Harm, Soul Wound, max HP pressure, damaged Soul Tether, damaged Soul Mooring, possession scar, memory fracture, curse/madness/spiritual contamination, Deviation symptom, Hidden Injury symptom, Heart Demon pressure, tribulation curse symptom, oath injury, bloodline injury, Dao-heart injury, or reincarnation complication;
- make Soul Check against harm DC;
- use Soul Treatment Result Bands;
- restores current HP only if paired with legal body-healing source;
- otherwise repairs root but not ordinary HP.

### 5.11 Deep Soul Repair

**Factor:** Deep Soul Repair  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Treats major Root Harm.

Default effect:

- requires Soul Repair;
- on success, reduce major harm by one stage, suppress until next trigger, or transform unstable symptom into stable Burden/treatment route;
- on success by 5+, also remove one minor linked symptom;
- on failure, reveal missing requirement;
- on failure by 5+, treatment backlash or harm complication.

### 5.12 Root Restoration

**Factor:** Root Restoration  
**Mandate / CP:** +7 / +7 CP

Ultimate root healing.

Default effect:

- requires Soul Repair and Deep Soul Repair;
- 1-hour ritual by default;
- on success, remove minor Root Harm, reduce major Root Harm, transform Deviation into stable route, repair Hidden Injury symptom, restore Soul Tether/Mooring, restore max HP pressure, or open recovery route for campaign-scale harm;
- on success by 5+, choose two compatible outputs;
- on failure, reveal missing requirement and stabilize target until next trigger if possible;
- current HP restoration requires body-healing source.

### 5.13 Soul Sight

**Factor:** Soul Sight  
**Mandate / CP:** +2 / +2 CP

Adds soul perception to a Sight-Quality Effect.

Default effect:

- source must be Sight-Quality Effect;
- make Soul Check or use source perception check against target Soul/Concealment/Illusion/Heaven/Fate DC;
- on success, detect Soul Presence;
- on success by 5+, identify one soul-layer state: missing, damaged, split, displaced, vessel-held, possessed, artificial, ghost, companion echo, ancestor echo, or Soul Wound category;
- on success by 10+, identify one treatment/countermeasure route;
- does not reveal full identity, full memories, complete sheet, or True Name by default.

### 5.14 Memory Mark

**Factor:** Memory Mark  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Creates or repairs Memory Mark.

Default effect:

- willing target: mark attaches;
- unwilling target: Intelligence or Charisma Soul Save;
- mark stores one memory category, oath memory, trauma imprint, reincarnation echo, or identity proof;
- duration 1 hour or scene;
- on failed save by 5+, target is unaware of mark;
- repair mode uses Soul Treatment Result Bands.

### 5.15 True-Name Pressure

**Factor:** True-Name Pressure  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Applies pressure through verified soul identifier.

Default effect:

- requires True Name, deep identifier, oath-name, soul title, or verified equivalent;
- target makes Charisma Soul Save;
- on failure, subtract one Soul Die from next Soul Save or suffer one written rider;
- on failed by 5+, target also gains visible soul mark until scene end;
- if identifier is false, Art fails and may backlash.

### 5.16 Death-Soul Boundary

**Factor:** Death-Soul Boundary  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Stabilizes or interacts with death boundary.

Default effect:

- Reaction or ritual when target dies, is dying, or becomes unreachable;
- make Soul Check against death/source/Heaven DC;
- on success, target's soul remains reachable until end of scene;
- on success by 5+, also preserve one Soul Tether or Memory Mark;
- on failure, learn what claimed or blocked the soul;
- this does not resurrect by itself.

### 5.17 Soul Transfer

**Factor:** Soul Transfer  
**Mandate / CP:** +5 / +5 CP

Moves soul or soul fragment between legal vessels.

GM-reviewed for permanent transfer.

Default effect:

- requires source soul, destination vessel, consent or Soul Save, and Soul Tether route;
- on success, transfer occurs for duration;
- on success by 5+, reduce transfer shock;
- on failure, transfer fails and reveals missing route;
- on failure by 5+, Soul Wound, possession complication, or vessel backlash.

### 5.18 Soul Space

**Factor:** Soul Space  
**Mandate / CP:** +4 / +4 CP

Creates internal soul-space or temporary inner chamber.

Default effect:

- create temporary Soul Space for memory, spirit echo, companion contact, root diagnosis, or internal trial;
- duration 1 minute combat or 1 hour ritual;
- entering unwilling target requires Soul Save;
- space has Soul DC and break route;
- cannot permanently evolve into full soul realm without reserved higher module.

### 5.20 Group Soul

**Factor:** Group Soul  
**Mandate / CP:** +3 / +3 CP

Affects legal targets up to Proficiency Bonus.

Default effect:

- same Soul Mode applies to each target;
- unwilling targets save separately;
- Soul Package split or applied separately as Art states;
- trigger frequency once per target per round.
